      <div type="clause" n="El. 13">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> El. 13</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 13" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="30" ed="#liebermann"/>Se mon se ðe his gewealdes monnan ófslea, swelte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.23"/> se deaðe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.24"/> Se ðe hine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.25"/> þonne nedes ófsloge oððe unwillu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> oððe ungewealdes, swelce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.26"/> hine God swa sende<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.27"/> on his honda, ⁊ he hine ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.28"/> ymbsyrede, sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.15"/> he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.29"/> feores wyrðe ⁊ folcryhtre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.30"/> bote<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.31"/>, gif he friðstowe gesece. Gif hwa ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> óf giernesse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.32"/> ⁊ gewealdes ófslea his þone nehstan þurh searwa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.33"/>, aluc ðu hine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.34"/> fro<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.35"/></hi> minu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> weofode<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.36"/>, to þam þæt he deaðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.37"/> swelte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 13" corresp="#wit-g-prol-only"><pb n="30" ed="#liebermann"/>Se man se ðe his gewealdes man ofslea, swelte se deaðe. Se ðe hyne ðonne nydes ofsloge oððe unwillu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> oððe ungewealdes, swylce hine God swa sende on hys handa, ⁊ he hyne ymbe ne sierede, sy he feores wyrþe ⁊ folcrihtre bote, gif he fryðstowa gesece. Gyf hwa þonne of geornnesse ⁊ gewealdes ofslea his ðone<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.2"/> nyehstan ðurh searwa, aluc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.3"/> ðu hine fra<hi rend="italic">m</hi> minan weofode, to ðam þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he deaðe swelte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 13" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="31" ed="#liebermann"/>Se man þe hys gewealdes man ofslea, swelte se deaþe. Se þe hine þonne neades ofslea oððe ungewylles oððe ungewealdes, swylce hyne God sende swa on his handa, ⁊ he him ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.1"/> syrwde ymbe, sy he feores wyrþe ⁊ folcrihtere bote, gif he friðstowe gesece. Gyf hwa þonne of geornnesse ⁊ gewealdes ofslea hys þone nyhstan þurh syrwunge, alúc þu hyne fra<hi rend="italic">m</hi> minu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> weofode, to ðam þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he deaþe swelte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="El. 13" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="31" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui percusserit hominem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.8"/> uolens occidere, morte moriatur. Qui autem non est insidiatus, sed Deus illum tradidit in manus eius, constituam tibi locum quo fugere debeat. Si quis per industriam occiderit proximum suum et per insidias, ab altari meo auelles<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.9"/> eum, ut moriatur.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="MP 13" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="236" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Se mon se ðe his gewealdes monnan ofslea, swelte se deaðe. Se ðe hine þonne nedes ofsloge oððe unwillum oððe ungewealdes, swelce hine God swa sende on his honda, ⁊ he hine ne ymbsyrede, sie he feores wyrðe ⁊ folcryhtre bote, gif he friðstowe gesece. Gif hwa ðonne of giernesse ⁊ gewealdes ofslea his þone nehstan þurh searwa, aluc ðu hine from minum weofode, to þam þæt he deaðe swelte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="31" ed="#liebermann"/>Der Mensch, welcher aus eigener Macht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.1"/> einen Menschen erschlägt, der sterbe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.2"/> Todes.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.3"/> Wer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.4"/> ihn aber aus Noth<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.5"/> erschlagen hat oder unfreiwillig oder ohne dafür zu können, wie Gott ihn so in seine Hände lieferte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.6"/>, und [wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.7"/>] er ihn nicht umlauert hat, so sei er des Lebens und volksrechtlicher Busse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.8"/> würdig, wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.9"/> er eine Schutzstätte findet. Wenn jemand dagegen aus Absicht und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.10"/> mit Willen seinen Nächsten durch Nachstellungen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.11"/> tödtet, so reisse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.12"/> du ihn fort von meinem Altare, auf dass er Todes sterbe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.13"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">The person who slays a person of his own will, let him die the death. But whoever slew him out of necessity, or unwillingly, or without being able to help it, as God so delivered him into his hands, and [if] he did not lie in wait for him, then let him be worthy of life and of compensation according to folk-law, if he reaches a place of sanctuary. If, on the other hand, someone kills his neighbour on purpose and willingly by lying in wait, then tear him away from my altar, so that he may die the death.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="237" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>The man who intentionally slays someone – let him die the death. However, he who slew him out of necessity or unwillingly or accidentally, as God sent to his hands, and he did not lie in wait [for his victim]: let him be worthy of life and of the remedy permitted by folk-law, if he should seek a place of refuge. But if someone with deliberation and intent slays his neighbor through guile, take him away from my altar, that he may die the death.</ab>
        <note type="passageSource">Exodus 21,12–14</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="31">Exodus 21.12; Exodus 21.13; Exodus 21.14</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">[21, 12] | [21, 13] | [21, 14]</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="236"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_5">Ine 5</ref> <quote>Compare Ine §5.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="237"><label>cf. (inward disposition of offender)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-16">Af El 16</ref> <quote>For Alfred, it is the inward disposition of the offender that is crucial ... cf. MP §16; Alfred §5.3 and §44.1 [L 42.1].</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="237"><label>cf. (inward disposition of offender)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_5-3">Af 5.3</ref> <quote>For Alfred, it is the inward disposition of the offender that is crucial ... cf. MP §16; Alfred §5.3 and §44.1 [L 42.1].</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="237"><label>cf. (inward disposition of offender)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_42-1">Af 42.1</ref> <quote>For Alfred, it is the inward disposition of the offender that is crucial ... cf. MP §16; Alfred §5.3 and §44.1 [L 42.1].</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="237"><label>parallel idiom</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_5">Ine 5</ref> <quote>The idiom is paralleled in Ine §5, which shows Alfred to have read this portion of Exodus in light of the sanctuary norms of his own day</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="333"><label>foreshadowed in</label> <ref target="clause:Af_36">Af 36</ref> <quote>the relevance of intent or its absence is foreshadowed in MP §13</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="375"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_5">Ine 5</ref> <quote>Compare MP §13 and Alfred §5.</quote></note>
