        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.37" n="37" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">30</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">deað <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">deað So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">31</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">31</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">patrem aut matrem, <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> h. v. (<hi rend="italic">zu El.</hi> 14 <hi rend="italic">hinüberspringend</hi>) <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">patrem aut matrem, instead of h. v. (skipping ahead to El. 14) Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">31</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eu. <hi rend="italic">Hk aus Vulg.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eu. Hk from Vulg.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">30</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">übergeschr. in anderer Tinte</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e written above in different ink</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">30</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verbessert aus</hi> abuc</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from abuc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Über die Form Sievers <hi rend="italic">Gram.</hi> § 320. Bessere die Übs. laut <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi>: ‘mit Willen’; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Absicht Z. 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On the form, Sievers <hi rend="italic">Gram.</hi> § 320. Correct the transl. according to <hi rend="italic">Wb</hi>: ‘wilfully’; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Absicht l. 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hinrichtung trifft nur den absichtlichen Totschlag gegen den Herrn laut Af El 49, 7. Vielleicht will der Satz, im Sinne erstarkender Polizeigewalt des Staates, den Schutz des Lebens der Bürger dem Systeme privater Blutrache zu entziehen beitragen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Execution applies only to intentional homicide against one’s lord, according to Af El 49, 7. Perhaps the sentence aims, in the spirit of the growing police power of the State, to help withdraw the protection of citizens’ lives from the system of private blood-feud</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">deaðe</hi> ist Instr.; die Vulg.-Redensart <hi rend="italic">morte mori</hi> ging auch in andere Germ. Volksrechte über, z. B. Lex Saxonum</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">deaðe</hi> is instr.; the Vulg. phrase <hi rend="italic">morte mori</hi> also passed into other Germanic folk-laws, e.g. Lex Saxonum</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Der Zusatz will den Exodus-Satz dem Agsä. Rechte angleichen. Aber auch ohne Asyl droht für Totschlag ohne Absicht (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 2a. 5) später nur Wergeld und höchstens Geldstrafe; <hi rend="italic">vgl. ebd.</hi> Notwehr</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The addition aims to adapt the Exodus sentence to A.-S. law. But even without sanctuary, homicide without intent (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 2a. 5) later incurs only wergild and at most a fine; <hi rend="italic">cf. ibid.</hi> Notwehr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Den bösen Willen in der Missetat betont Ælfred, im Ggs. zu Urgerm. Strafrecht, auch indem er zu Ps. 13, 6 über Sünde des Blutvergiessens zur Übersetzung hinzufügt: <hi rend="italic">for yflum willum; vgl.</hi> Wichmann in <hi rend="italic">Anglia</hi> 11 (1888) 88</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ælfred emphasizes the evil will in the misdeed, in contrast to Proto-Germanic criminal law, also by adding to his translation of Ps. 13, 6, on the sin of bloodshed: <hi rend="italic">for yflum willum; cf.</hi> Wichmann in <hi rend="italic">Anglia</hi> 11 (1888) 88</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘fallen liess’ Schmid; eig. ‘schickte’</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘let fall’ Schmid; properly ‘sent’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> über dies Anakoluth Wülfing <hi rend="italic">Syntax</hi> I 410</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> on this anacoluthon Wülfing <hi rend="italic">Syntax</hi> I 410</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> Ine 5</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> Ine 5</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.9" n="9" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Im Ggs. zur Exodus lässt Af die Asyle schon vorhanden sein. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Asyl 3; Plummer <hi rend="italic">Alfred</hi> 153</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In contrast to Exodus, Af assumes the sanctuaries to be already in existence. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Asyl 3; Plummer <hi rend="italic">Alfred</hi> 153</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.10" n="10" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Pleonastische Synonyma für Abstrakta begegnen in Ælfreds Übersetzung häufig: Zeichen tastender Anfängerschaft. — Dieser Exodus-Vers beförderte die Ausscheidung des Mordes aus dem Totschlag im Germanischen Strafrecht, und noch 1469 wird er in Schottland zitiert, als man den Mörder vom Asyl ausschliesst; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Maitland <hi rend="italic">Malice aforethought</hi> in <hi rend="italic">Coll. papers</hi> I 324</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Pleonastic synonyms for abstract nouns occur frequently in Ælfred’s translation: a sign of a beginner’s groping. — This verse of Exodus promoted the separation of murder from homicide in Germanic criminal law, and it is still quoted in Scotland in 1469, when the murderer is excluded from sanctuary; <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> Maitland <hi rend="italic">Malice aforethought</hi> in <hi rend="italic">Coll. papers</hi> I 324</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.11" n="11" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H modernisiert</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H modernizes</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.12" n="12" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nicht ‘schliesse aus’; es gibt zwei Wörter <hi rend="italic">lucan</hi> ‘schliessen’ und ‘reissen, jäten’; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Wright <hi rend="italic">Dial. dict.: louk;</hi> mndd. <hi rend="italic">luken</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘shut out’; there are two words <hi rend="italic">lucan</hi>, ‘to shut’ and ‘to pull, to weed’; <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> Wright <hi rend="italic">Dial. dict.: louk;</hi> MLG <hi rend="italic">luken</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_El-to-13.lnote.de.13" n="13" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ælfreds eigenes Recht harmoniert nicht mit solchem Asyl; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 3. 5, 4. 13</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ælfred’s own law does not harmonize with such sanctuary; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 3. 5, 4. 13</seg></note>
      </div>
